The macOS options of the bcm2837 machine, as macOS-DroidVM boots macOS 27.0.1 (26A434) with them: System V IPC, sendfile,
the external resolver, firmlinks (APFS stitches the System and Data volumes of the one container), searchfs, file leases,
audit, CSR with its configuration from the device tree, supplemental signatures and a second static trust cache; and
vfs_quota.c always built (the HFS and APFS quota KPIs the macOS kexts bind to) without turning on quota checking itself.
The rest of the machine file stays as the iPadOS build reads it; only the macOS profile applies this patch.
Upstream UniXNU's macos-machine-config (27.3) takes more of MASTER.arm64.MacOSX (quota, volfs, mnt_suid, rosv_startup,
mount_vm, prebootrecovery, appledouble, nullfs, arm_pfz); those are left out until a macOS-DroidVM boot needs them --
rosv_startup in particular changes how the root volume group is mounted.
From macOS-DroidVM patches/xnu-12377/0007, 0023 (vfs_quota.c), 0036 and 0046 (lateautumn233).

